$DATUM (2S)-5-tert-Butoxycarbonylamino-2-pthalimidopentane-1-ol. A mixture of 9
(50.0 mg, 0.142 mmol) and 10% Pd/C (10 mg) in MeOH (2 mL) were vigorously
stirred under H2 atmosphere at room temperature for 1 h. The catalyst was
filtered off through Celite pad, and the filtrate was concentrated in
vacuo. A solution of the residue and N-carboethoxy phthalimide (34.2 mg,
0.156 mmol) in THF (2 mL) was treated with sodium carbonate (16.6 mg,
0.156 mmol) and stirred at room temperature for 24 h. After AcOH (18.7
µL, 0.32 mmol) was added, the mixture was diluted with AcOEt (50 mL),
which was washed with H2O and saturated aq. NaCl. The organic phase was
dried (Na2SO4), filtered and concentrated in vacuo. The residue was
purified by silica gel column chromatography (2×10 cm, 43% AcOEt/hexane)
to afford the title compound (45.3 mg, 92% over 2 steps) as a white foam.
[α]22D 0.49 (c 1.04, CHCl3); 1H NMR(CD3OD, 500 MHz) δ 7.86 (m, 2H,
phthaloyl), 6.62 (br s, 1H, NH-Boc), 4.35 (ddd, 1H, H-2, J2,1a = 5.7,
J2,1b = 11.6, J2,3 = 15.5 Hz), 4.08 (t, 1H, H-1a, J1a,2 = J1a,1b = 11.0
Hz), 3.77 (dd, 1H, H-5, J5,4 = 7.5, J5a,5b = 14.3 Hz), 2.02 (m, 1H,
H-3a), 1.73 (m, 1H, H-3b, J3b,3a = 16.5 Hz), 1.46 (m, 2H, H-4), 1.42 (s,
9H, tBu); 13C NMR (CD3OD, 125 MHz) δ 168.9, 157.2, 134.0, 131.9, 122.7,
78.5, 61.5, 53.8, 39.6, 27.4, 26.6, 25.3; FABMS-LR m/z 349 [(M+ H)+];
FABMS-HR calcd for C18H25N2O5 349.1764, found 349.1753.
