$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
(3'S,4S,5''S,9'S,11'S)-1'''-{[4-({[3,5-bis(trifluoromethyl)phenyl]carbamoyl}amino)phenyl]carbonyl}-4''-[(2,4-dimethoxyphenyl)methyl]-1''-{[2-(hydroxymethyl)phenyl]methyl}-2,2',3'',5,6'',8'-hexaoxo-1-phenyl-3-(pyridin-4-ylmethyl)trispiro[imidazolidine-4,5'-[1,7]diazatricyclo[7.3.0.03,7]dodecane-11',2''-piperazine-5'',3'''-pyrrolidine]-5'''-carboxylic
acid 15a: Activation of carboxylic acid 14a has been done using the
following procedure: In a flame dried vial, 4-urea benzoic acid 14a ( 98
mg, 250 μmol) and HATU (90 mg, 237 μmol) were dissolved in 4 ml dry DMF
under argon, then DIPEA ( 87 μl, 500 μmol ) was added. The reaction
mixture was allowed to stir for 5 min at room temperature. The resulting
solution was combined with the solution of trimer 13 (249 mg, 250 μmol)
in 1 ml dry DMF. The reaction mixture was allowed to stir for 8 hours at
room temperature. At this point to remove Alloc protecting group, a
solution of Pd(PPh3)4 (29 mg, 25 μmmol) and BH3.NMe2 ( 35 mg, 1.5 mmmol)
in 1 ml dry DCM was added and The deprotection was allowed to continue
for 8 hours at room temperature. To quench the reaction and get free
hydroxyl, 4mL 1M HCl was added and the solution was stirred for two
hours. After which the product was reverse phase purified using C18
column with a gradient of 5-95% H2O/ACN with 0.1% formic acid 13.
(3'S,4S,5''S,9'S,11'S)-1'''-{[3-({[3,5-bis(trifluoromethyl)phenyl]carbamoyl}amino)phenyl]carbonyl}-4''-[(2,4-dimethoxyphenyl)methyl]-1''-{[2-(hydroxymethyl)phenyl]methyl}-2,2',3'',5,6'',8'-hexaoxo-1-phenyl-3-(pyridin-4-ylmethyl)trispiro[imidazolidine-4,5'-[1,7]diazatricyclo[7.3.0.03,7]dodecane-11',2''-piperazine-5'',3'''-pyrrolidine]-5'''-carboxylic
acid 15b: The same procedure has been used for spirolgozyme 15a using
3-urea benzoic acid. Yield 74mg, 23%. 1H NMR (500 MHz, DMSO-d6, 1% TFA
added, 345 K, δ) 9.48 (s, 1H), 9.09 (s, 1H), 8.77 (s, 2H), 8.13 (s, 2H),
7.97-7.96 (d, 2H, J = 5.5), 7.56-7.48 (m, 7H), 7.42-7.79 (m, 1H),
7.35-7.33 (d, 1H, J = 7.5), 7.32-7.29 (t, 1H, J = 8), 7.22-7.19 (m, 2H),
7.04-7.02 (d, 1H, J = 8.5), 6.97-6.95 (t, 2H, J = 7.5), 6.59 (d, 1H, J =
2.5), 6.53-6.51 (dd, 1H, J = 1.5, 8.5), 4.87 (s, 2H), 4.73-4.57 (m, 7H),
4.53 (s, 2H), 4.00-3.65 (m, 12H), 2.86-2.82 (dd, 1H, J = 9.5, 14),
2.73-2.69 (dd, 1H, J = 7.5, 13.5), 2.67-2.62 (dd, 1H, J = 7.5, 13.5),
2.56-2.54 (m, 1H), 2.46-2.42 (dd, 2H, J = 8.5, 13.5). 13C NMR (From HMBC,
125 MHz, DMSO-d6, , 1% TFA added, 345 K, δ) 172.56, 171.72, 168.11,
167.89, 167.45, 164.78, 164.12, 159.30, 156.62, 156.18, 155.11, 154.28,
142.21, 141.39, 138.67, 137.89, 137.56, 136.0, 134.32, 131.23, 127.89,
