$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Pro-Gly-Pro-Gly production. DCC (5.5 g, 27 mmol) was added to a solution
of 4.3 g (0.02 mol) Boc-Pro-Gly-OH and 4.4 g (0.022 mol) TFA ·
Pro-Gly-OBzl in 65 mL of methylene chloride, cooled to -10°C, and the
mixture was stirred for 2 h at this temperature, and then left for 16
hours at 20°C. The precipitated dicyclohexylurea was filtered off, the
solvent was removed under vacuum, and the remaining oil was dissolved in
130 mL of ethyl acetate and washed successively with 1 M hydrochloric
acid, water, 1 M sodium bicarbonate, and a 25% solution of NaCl. The
organic phase was dried with anhydrous magnesium sulfate for 1 h. When
the solution became clear, ethyl acetate was evaporated on a rotary
evaporator. Protections were removed (benzyl ether-by hydrogenation in a
stream of dry hydrogen with the addition of palladium black,
t-butyloxycarbonyl protection-50% TFA in CH2Cl2), then unprotected
peptide H-Pro-Gly-Pro-Gly-OH was converted to acetate form using a cation
exchanger Amberlist A-21. Purification was carried out by
recrystallization from methanol with dry diethyl ether. Yield 75%. mp
93°C, [α]22D 89.63° (c 1, methanol), Rf 0.374 (E), 0.245 (F).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Proteolysis of simple glyprolines by leucine aminopeptidase and enzymes
from nasal mucus, brain membranes, and blood of rats
