$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Tetramer 19. Catalytic hydrogenation of 18
(232 mg, 0.393 mmol) led to the corresponding amine, which was mixed with
triethylamine (0.5 mL, 1.5 equiv.) in CH2Cl2 (20 mL) and then treated
with the acid chloride, prepared from acid 10 (200 mg, 0.313 mmol) and
oxalyl chloride (0.5 mL), and dissolved in CH2Cl2 (10 mL). The reaction
mixture was stirred at room temperature overnight and was then washed
with brine, dried over anhydrous Na2SO4. After removal of solvent, the
residue was triturated with CH2Cl2/n-hexane to provide the tetramer as a
white solid 19 (235 mg, yield 62%). Hexamer 22. This oligomer was
prepared from pentamer 21 and acid chloride 6 based on procedures we
described before.1 Yield, 71%; 1H-NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3):δ (s, 1H), 9.92
(s, 1H), 9.71 (s, 1H), 9.60 (s, 1H), 9.25 (s, 1H), 9.11 (s, 1H), 9.06 (s,
1H), 8.90 (s, 1H), 8.46 (d, J = 2.5 Hz, 1H), 8.03 (s, 1H), 7.63 (d, J =
6.5 Hz, 1H), 6.58 (s, 1H), 6.51 (s, 1H), 6.47 (s, 1H), 6.44 (s, 1H), 6.40
(s, 1H), 6.36 (s, 1H), 6.30 (s, 1H), 6.24 (s, 1H), 5.10 (d, J= 15 Hz,
1H), 4.52 (d, J= 15 Hz, 1H), 4.20 (m, 4H), 3.93 (d, 8H), 3.92 (s, 27H),
3.86 (d, 8H), 2.27 (m, 2H), 2.09 (m, 2H), 1.67 (m, 2H), 1.43 (m, 4H),
0.90 (d, 36); 13C NMR (75.5 MHz, CDCl3) 173.78, 166.41, 163.28, 162.18,
160.46, 158.33, 157.60, 157.13, 153.54, 151.01, 149.04, 146.04, 145.66,
135.86, 133.74, 131.67, 125.99, 125.06, 123.81, 119.84, 104.61, 98.61,
70.51, 70.37, 69.43, 56.39, 55.86, 55.72, 38.95, 38.88, 29.12, 28.84,
28.54, 25.51, 23.05, 20.18, 19.97, 19.87, 19.74, 19.60; MS (ESI) m/z ,
calcd for C88H114N6O25Na+ 1678.7, 1677.5, 1673.3, 1655.4, 1493.4, 1392.5.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Improving Foldamer Synthesis through Protecting Group Induced Unfolding
of Aromatic Oligoamides
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
