$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Tripeptide 21. Dipeptide 20 (420 mg, 0.77 mmol) was dissolved in MeOH (6
mL), Pd(OH)2/C (84 mg) was added. The mixture was hydrogenated at 1 atm
for 6 h, then filtrated, concentrated under reduced pressure to give
amine 12 as a white foam. The residue was subjected to the next reaction
without further purification. The above amine and D-Fmoc-Leu-OH (325 mg,
0.92 mmol) was dissolved in dry CH2Cl2 (6 mL), then DIPEA (0.26 mL, 1.54
mmol), HOBt (124 mg, 0.92 mmol) and EDCI (177 mg, 0.92 mmol) were added
subsequently. The reaction mixture was stirred overnight and the solvent
was removed in vacuo. The residue was dissolved in EtOAc, washed
successively with 1 M HCl, sat. NaHCO3, brine, dried over Na2SO4,
filtrated and concentrated under reduced pressure. The residue was
purified by flash chromatography eluting with 3:2 ethyl acetate/petroleum
ether to give tripeptide 21 (517 mg, 90% for 2 steps) as a white foam.
[α]D 26.9 = +28.7 (c 1.0, CHCl3); IR (film) 3268, 2954, 2857, 1651, 1506,
1253, 1039, 740 cm-1; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 0.05 (m, 6H), 0.90 (m,
15H), 1.36 (d, J = 6.4 Hz, 3H), 1.65 (m, 9H), 2.05 (m, 1H), 2.23 (m, 2H),
2.80 (m, 4H), 3.08 (m, 1H), 3.83 (s, 1H), 4.30 (m, 4H), 5.17 (d, J = 6.8
Hz, 1H), 5.35 (m, 2H), 5.51 (d, J = 8.8 Hz, 1H), 6.51 (s, 1H), 7.10 (d, J
= 6.8 Hz, 1H), 7.29 (m, 2H), 7.37 (m, 2H), 7.58 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 2H), 7.74
(d, J = 7.6 Hz, 2H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ -4.9, -4.7, 18.1, 19.2,
22.2, 23.2, 23.3, 25.0, 25.5, 25.8, 25.9, 26.1, 33.3, 42.6, 45.5, 46.7,
47.4, 47.9, 49.1, 53.4, 53.8, 54.6, 56.8, 57.3, 58.8, 62.5, 63.3, 67.2,
120.1, 125.4, 127.3, 127.8, 141.5, 144.0, 144.3, 171.2, 174.0, 175.1,
175.8; ESIMS m/z 749.4 (M + H)+; HRMS calcd. for C40H61N6O6Si (M + H)+
requires 749.4416, found 749.4410.
