$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM First, 10 was directly coupled with L-proline benzyl ester in the
presence of BOP to give a diastereomeric mixture of dipeptides that was
used for the next reaction without additional purification. Reduction of
the benzyl ester followed by WSC-mediated cyclization afforded the
cis-fused product 7 (9% from 10), which has the natural relative and
absolute configuration for the synthesis of spirotryprostatin A, plus the
trans-fused substance (12, 10% from 10), which was converted into
9-epi-spirotryprostatin A. 7, yield 9%; 12, yield 10% 7: [α]25D = -60.0
(CHCl3, c=0.33); 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ CHCl3: 0.93 (s, 6H), 1.86-2.24
(m, 5H), 2.30-2.66 (m, 3H), 2.83 (s, 3H), 3.57 (dd, J= 5.4, 8.2 Hz, 2H),
3.79 (s, 3H), 4.20-4.27 (m, 2H), 4.77 (t, J= 8.8 Hz, 1H), 6.43 (s, 1H),
6.54 (d, J= 8.4 Hz, 1H), 7.04 (d, J= 8.4 Hz, 1H), 7.64 (bs, 1H); 13C NMR
(100 MHz, CDCl3) δ CHCl3: 23.3, 23.6, 24.9, 27.9, 30.0, 34.9, 40.8, 45.0,
48.7, 55.5, 58.4, 59.8, 61.4, 74.0, 97.1, 106.5, 121.4, 126.3, 142.0,
160.2, 166.7, 168.1, 181.4; IR (NaCl/neat) 1716, 1665, 1633, 1506, 1461,
1343, 1193, 1157, 732 cm-1; HRMS (FAB+) calcd for C23H30O5N3 (m/z)
428.2185, found (m/z) 428.2193. 12: [α]25D = -77.0 (CHCl3, c=0.2); 1H NMR
(400 MHz, CDCl3) δ CHCl3: 1.02 (s, 3H), 1.19 (s, 3H), 1.76- 1.86 (m, 2H),
1.87-2.08 (m, 3H), 2.41-2.53 (m, 3H), 2.93 (s, 3H), 3.40 (ddd, J= 3.6,
9.4, 12.4 Hz, 1H), 3.80 (s, 3H), 3.94 (dt, J= 12.4, 8.3 Hz, 1H), 4.22
(dd, J= 5.4, 11.4 Hz, 1H), 4.61 (t, J= 8.8 Hz, 1H), 4.81 (t, J= 6.8 Hz,
1H), 6.47 (s, 1H), 6.54 (d, J= 8.2 Hz, 1H), 7.09 (d, J= 8.2 Hz, 1H), 7.58
(bs, 1H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ CHCl3: 21.7, 23.2, 24.7, 30.0, 40.6,
