$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To a solution of 9 (1.689 g, 5.20 mmol) in methanol (20 mL) was added 10%
Pd-C (162 mg). The mixture was stirred under H2 (1 atm) at ambient
temperature for 3.5 h. The Pd-C catalyst was filtrated off. The filtrate
was concentrated to give an amine. To a solution of this amine in dry
CH2Cl2-DMF (1:1 v/v, 30 mL) were added N-phthaloyl-Lphenylpropanoic acid
(1.24 g, 4.20 mmol), HOBt (567 mg, 4.20 mmol), EDC (805 mg, 4.20 mmol)
and N-methylmorpholine (1.72 mL, 12.6 mmol) at 0 °C. After completion of
the addition, the mixture was stirred at ambient temperature overnight,
diluted with EtOAc (100 mL), washed successively with 1 N HCl, saturated
Na2CO3, and brine, dried over anhydrous Na2SO4 and then concentrated. The
residue was purified by column chromatography (2:3 EtOAc/PE) on silica
gel to give 10 as a white foam (1.572 g, 92%). [α]D 20 -5.1° (c 0.97,
CHCl3). 1H NMR (CDCl3, 300 MHz) δ 7.79-7.77 (m, 2H), 7.72- 7.68 (m, 2H),
7.17-7.7.11 (m, 5H), 6.89 (d, J = 7.5 Hz, 1H), 5.12 (dd, J = 10.6, 5.8
Hz, 1H), 4.64-4.57 (m, 1H), 4.29 (t, J = 5.6 Hz, 1H), 3.71 (s, 1H),
3.62-3.48 (m, 2H), 3.19 (s, 3H), 3.18 (s, 3H), 1.92-1.56 (m, 4H); FT-IR
(film): 3350, 3053, 2952, 1777, 1716, 1686, 1383 cm-1; ESI-MS m/z
491.3([M+Na]+). Anal calcd for C25H28N2O7 C 64.09, H 6.07, N 5.98; found
C 64.36, H 6.25 N 6.23.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Design, Synthesis, and Evaluation of Tricyclic, Conformationally
Constrained Small-Molecule Mimetics of Second Mitochondria-Derived
Activator of Caspases
