$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Step A: Intermediate 2S (559.3 mg, 1.59 mmol) was dissolved in THF (40
ml) and HCl in 1, 4-dioxane (4.0 M, 597 ul, 1.3 eq) was added. The
mixture was transferred into a Parr shaker precharged with Pd black, high
surface area (224.2 mg) under nitrogen. The mixture was hydrogenated
under 45 psi H2 pressure at 23 °C for 24 h then filtered. The filtrate
was concentrated and triturated with MTBE (10 ml). The unpurified
(S)-2-amino-5-tertbutoxy-4,5-dioxopentanoic acid (420.9 mg), which was
used without further purification. Step B:
2,2-diphenylisobenzofuro[5,6-d][1,3]dioxole-5,7-dione (286.9 mg, 0.83
mmol) and (S)-2-amino-5-tert-butoxy-4,5-dioxopentanoic acid (303 mg, 0.84
mmol) were heated in 3 mL pyridine at 90 °C for 1.5 h then concentrated
in vacuo. The residue was partitioned between dichloromethane (10 ml) and
aqueous citric acid (5 ml, 75g/L). The aqueous layer was extracted with
dichloromethane (2 x 5 ml) and the combined organic layers were
concentrated in vacuo.
(S)-5-tert-butoxy-2-(5,7-dioxo-2,2-diphenyl-5H-[1,3]dioxolo[4,5-f]isoindol-6(7H)-yl)-4,5-dioxopentanoic
acid (563.2 mg), which was used without purification. Step C: To
Intermediate 1 (332.1 mg, 0.65 mmol) and unpurified
(S)-5-tert-butoxy-2-(5,7-dioxo-2,2-diphenyl-5H-[1,3]dioxolo[4,5-f]isoindol-6(7H)-yl)-4,5-dioxopentanoic
acid (554.4 mg) in 6 mL acetonitrile was added dicyclohexylcarbodiimide
(188.0 mg, 0.91 mmol). The reaction mixture was stirred at 23 °C for 16 h
then filtered. The filtrate was purified by silica gel chromatography,
eluting first with gradient n-heptane/EtOAc:DCM (1:3) to remove
impurities, then gradient DCM/ DCM:IPA (90:10). (4S)-tert-butyl
2-((S)-4-((Z)-2-(1-tert-butoxy-2-methyl-1-oxopropan-2-yloxyimino)-2-(2-(tert-butoxycarbonylamino)thiazol-4-yl)acetamido)-3-oxoisoxazolidin-2-yl)-4-(5,7-dioxo-2,2-diphenyl-5H-[1,3]dioxolo[4,5-f]isoindol-6(7H)-yl)-5-oxotetrahydrofuran-2-carboxylate
(151.4 mg, 22 %) as a white solid. LCMS m/z 1039.6 (M+H). 1H NMR (400
MHz, METHANOL-d 4) δ ppm 7.53 -7.60 (m, 5 H), 7.38 -7.47 (m, 8 H), 5.02
-5.52 (m, 2 H), 4.75 -4.88 (m, 1 H), 4.25 -4.46 (m, 1 H), 3.26 -3.44 (m,
1 H), 2.80 -2.97 (m, 1 H), 1.51 -1.58 (m, 24 H), 1.47 (s, 9 H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Parr shaker used in stage 1
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Siderophore receptor-mediated uptake of lactivicin analogs in
Gram-negative bacteria
