$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Step A: Intermediate 2R (625 mg, 1.78 mmol) was dissolved in THF (50 ml)
and HCl in 1, 4-dioxane (4.0 M, 586 ul, 1.3 eq) was added. The reaction
was transferred into a Parr shaker precharged with Pd black, high surface
area (286.6 mg) under nitrogen. The mixture was hydrogenated under 45 psi
H2 pressure at 23 °C for 25 h. The catalyst was filtered off and the
filtrate was concentrated and triturated with n-pentane/hexanes (3:1, 40
ml). (R)-2-amino-5-tert-butoxy-4,5-dioxopentanoic acid (510 mg) as a
solid, which was used without further purification. To a suspension of
1,5-bis(benzyloxy)-4-oxo-1,4-dihydropyridine-2-carboxylic acid (726.8 mg,
1.9 mmol) in 20 mL of dichloromethane was added DMF (13.7 ul), followed
by oxalyl chloride (166 ul, 1.9 mmol) at 0 °C. The reaction was stirred
at 0 °C for 50 min to generate a stock solution of
1,5-bis(benzyloxy)-4-oxo-1,4-dihydropyridine-2-carbonyl chloride which
was used without isolation. To unpurified
(R)-amino-5-tert-butoxy-4,5-dioxopentanoic acid (495 mg) in 10 mL
dichloromethane was added the a freshly prepared solution of
1,5-bis(benzyloxy)-4-oxo-1,4-dihydropyridine-2-carbonyl chloride (1.66
mmol in 20 ml of dichloromethane), followed by DBU (620 ul, 4.15 mmol) at
0 °C. The reaction mixture was stirred from 0 °C to 23 °C for 16 h. A
solution of 7.5 g of citric acid anhydrate in 100 ml of water was
prepared. The citric acid solution (30 ml) was added to the reaction
mixture and the organic layer was separated. The aqueous layer was
extracted with dichloromethane (2 x 30 ml) and the combined organic
layers were washed with additional citric acid solution (10 ml) then
concentrated in vacuo. The residue was triturated with n-pentane (30 ml)
and MTBE (2 x 20 ml).
(R)-2-(1,5-bis(benzyloxy)-4-oxo-1,4-dihydropyridine-2-carboxamido)-5-tert-butoxy-4,5-dioxopentanoic
acid (725 mg), which was used in the next step directly without
purification. Step C: To Intermediate 1 (361.3 mg, 0.70 mmol) and
unpurified
(R)-2-(1,5-bis(benzyloxy)-4-oxo-1,4-dihydropyridine-2-carboxamido)-5-tert-butoxy-4,5-dioxopentanoic
acid (725 mg) in dichloromethane (12 ml) was added
dicyclohexylcarbodiimide (201.5 mg, 0.98 mmol). The reaction mixture was
stirred at 23 °C for 4.5 h then filtered. The filtrate was purified by
silica gel chromatography, eluting first with gradient
n-heptane/EtOAc:DCM (1:3) to remove side products, then gradient DCM/
DCM:IPA (90:10). (4R)-tert-butyl
4-(1,5-bis(benzyloxy)-4-oxo-1,4-dihydropyridine-2-carboxamido)-2-((S)-4-((Z)-2-(1-tert-butoxy-2-methyl-1-oxopropan-2-yloxyimino)-2-(2-(tert-butoxycarbonylamino)thiazol-4-yl)acetamido)-3-oxoisoxazolidin-2-yl)-5-oxotetrahydrofuran-2-carboxylate
(190.9 mg, combined yield for three steps is 14 %) as a white solid. LCMS
m/z 1046.3 (M+H). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CHLOROFORM-d) δ ppm 8.04-8.08 (two
pairs of d, 1 H), 7.21 -7.47 (m, 11 H), 6.83 and 6.84 (two s, 1 H), 6.46
and 6.51 (two s, 1 H), 4.80 -5.32 (m, 7 H), 4.16 -4.34 (m, 1 H), 3.24
-3.52 (m, 1 H), 2.62 -2.99 (m, 1 H), 1.43 -1.62 (m, 33 H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM parr shaker used in stage 1
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Siderophore receptor-mediated uptake of lactivicin analogs in
Gram-negative bacteria
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
