$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: (S)-N 6-tert-Butoxycarbonyl-N
4-acetyl-4-azalysine (30a). A solution of 29a (0.384 g, 0.90 mmol) in
methanol (10 mL) was hydrogenated at room temperature with stirring in
the presence of 10% Pd-C (0.038 g). On completion, the reaction mixture
was filtered through a Celite pad and the filtrate evaporated to dryness
(S)-N 6-Butoxycarbonyl-N 4-propionyl-N 4-azalysine (30b) Catalytic
hydrogenation of 29b (0.430 g, 0.98 mmol) using 10% Pd-C (0.043 g) in
methanol (10 mL) in the procedure described for 30a gave the title
compound 30b, which was recrystallized from MeOH/diethyl ether to give
the final product (0.285 g, 96%) as a white solid mp 138-140 °C;
(MeOH:acetic acid, 5:0.5) R f = 0.47; [α]D 26 -13.8° (c 0.29, MeOH); ν
max (KBr) 3401, 1694 cm-1; δ H (MeOH-d 4) 1.15 (3H, t, J 7.4, COCH2CH3),
1.46 (9H, s, C(CH3)3), 2.51 (2H, q, J 1.6, COCH2CH3), 3.10-3.65 (6H, m, 3
x CH2), 3.75-4.00 (1H, m, CαH); m/z (ES-MS) 304.3 (MH+), calcd. 304.2.
