$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: To a solution of 5 (60 mg, 0.070 mmol) in
CH2Cl2 (6 ml), PhSiH3 (18 μl, 0.141 mmol) and tetrakis
(triphenylphosphine) palladium (6 mg, 0.005 mmol) was added, the
resulting mixture was stirred at room temperature for 10 min, then Na2CO3
was added and the aqueous phase was extracted with CH2Cl2. The organic
layer was washed with brine, dried with Na2SO4 afforded the crude amine.
The resulting amine and the acid 6 (23 mg, 0.073 mmol) was dissolved in
CH2Cl2 (6 ml), EDC (14 mg, 0.073 mmol), HOBt (10 mg, 0.073 mmol) was
added. The resulting mixture was stirred for 2 h. It was then diluted
with CH2Cl2 and washed with sat. Na2CO3 and brine. The organic layer was
dried over Na2SO4 and concentrated. Chromatography (Acetone-Petroleum
ether, 1:2) of the residue gave 4 (60 mg, 80%) as a white solid.
According to the procedure for the conversion of 5 into 4，19 (40 mg,
0.047 mmol) was transformed into 20 (40 mg, 80%). Major isomer: [α]D25 =
-28.5 (c = 2.4, CH2Cl2); νmax (film)/cm-1 3396, 2970, 2931, 2114, 1697,
1647, 1512, 1452, 1246, 1117, 737; 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.45-7.32
(m, 7H), 7.21 (s, 1H), 7.12 (d, J = 8.7 Hz, 2H), 6.91 (d, J = 8.7 Hz,
2H), 6.85 (d, J = 10.2 Hz, 1H), 6.06 (m, 1H), 5.56 (m, 1H), 5.46 (d, J =
7.5 Hz, 1H), 5.04 (s, 2H), 4.99 (m, 1H), 4.60 (m, 1H), 4.52 (m, 1H),
4.40-4.31 (m, 3H), 4.06 (d, J = 9.9 Hz, 1H), 3.70 (m, 4H), 3.58 (m, 1H);
3.51 (m, 1H), 3.32 (s, 3H), 3.13 (m, 2H), 2.22-1.76 (m, 8H), 2.19 (s,
3H), 2.10 (s, 3H), 1.61 (m, 1H), 0.98 (m, 2H), 0.89 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 3H),
0.80 (d, J = 6.9 Hz, 3H); 13C NMR (75MHz, CDCl3): δ 172.6, 171.2, 170.4,
169.9, 168.7, 167.6, 167.5, 158.1, 155.4, 151.2, 144.9, 137.0, 135.6,
133.2, 130.5, 128.7, 128.1, 127.7, 125.5, 117.0, 115.1, 80.1, 72.9, 70.1,
66.3, 62.4, 60.9, 60.4, 59.4, 56.2, 53.2, 52.0, 49.7, 47.7, 47.5, 40.7,
34.9, 29.8, 28.5, 25.2, 25.0, 22.7, 17.5, 15.7, 14.2, 12.1; HRMS (ESI):
calcd. for C54H70N10O11SNa [M+Na]+, 1089.4844. Found: [M+Na]+, 1089.4858
(1.3 ppm error).
