$DATUM Synthesis of G4G BocNH-G(Cbz)-OH (0.50 g, 0.92 mmol), HBTU (0.43 g, 0.99
mmol) and DIPEA (0.33 mL, 1.89 mmol) were combined in dry DMF (2.00 mL)
and allowed to stir for 1 h at room temperature. To this mixture, 7 (0.07
g, 0.36 mmol) was added and the reaction was stirred for 4 h further at
room temperature. The solvent was then evaporated and the residue dried
for 3 h at 40°C in a vacuum oven. Column chromatography (SiO2;
CHCl3/MeOH; 100/0, 98/2, …, 90/10; crude material packed onto silica from
methanol) of the resulting crude material afforded a tan solid which was
then precipitated out of a methanol/ether mixture to yield G(Cbz)4G(Cbz).
G(Cbz)4G(Cbz) was suspended in methanol (1 mL) and methylene chloride (1
mL). Commercial 10% - Pd/C catalyst (0.12 g) was added. The mixture was
stirred at room temperature under H2 gas overnight. The reaction was then
filtered from the catalyst; the catalyst was washed and heated to reflux
in methanol. The catalyst was filtered off and the methanol was
evaporated down to a small amount and the two solvent fractions were
combined. The product was then precipitated using ethyl ether. It was
filtered and dried under vacuum to yield G4G (19.5% overall yield). 1H
NMR (d 6 -DMSO, 600 MHz, rotamers designated ri and rii): δ ri/rii
8.23/7.89 (2H, s, NH), 7.49 (2H, s, G-H8), ri/rii 7.03/6.76 (2H, m, NH),
ri/rii 4.92/4.79 (4H, s, CH2), ri/rii 4.09/3.97 (4H, s, CH2), ri and rii
3.47 – 3.01 (47H, m, PNA CH2 and TEG CH2), 1.36 – 1.15 (36H, m, t-Bu and
alk-CH2). 13C NMR (600 MHz, d 6 -DMSO): 167.7, 167.4, 166.7, 157.1,
155.7, 155.5, 153.9, 151.6, 137.7, 115.9, 79.1, 78.0, 71.2, 69.8, 69.6,
69.5, 67.3, 58.0, 54.0, 52.9, 50.1, 48.7, 47.2, 43.4, 43.2, 29.1, 28.3,
28.2, 28.1, 26.5. MALDI MS (α-cyano hydroxycinnamic acid): 1126 [M+H]+.
