$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for the Arylation of Dipeptides (Tables 1 and 2). To a
microwave tube (5 mL) was added the substrate (0.2 mmol), Pd(OAc)2 (0.005
or 0.01 mmol as indicated in Table 1 or 2), AgOAc (0.24 mmol), ArI (0.3
mmol), KF (0.6 mmol), and HFIP (1 mL) in air. The tube was sealed and
heated to 100 °C. The mixture was stirred for 20 h at 100 °C. Upon
completion, the reaction mixture was cooled to room temperature. To the
mixture was added acetic acid (0.3 mL) and EtOAc (3 mL). The mixture was
filtered through a short Celite pad, and the filtrate was concentrated
under reduced pressure. The resulting mixture was purified by preparative
TLC, typically using hexane/ethyl acetate/HOAc mixtures as the eluent.
The arylated product as a solid. The arylated product was typically
obtained as a single diastereomer (d.r. > 20:1), as evidenced by 1H NMR
and 13C NMR. Product: 2a; White solid (82% mono + 8% di). 1H NMR (400M
Hz, CDCl3): δ 7.80-7.77 (m, 2 H), 7.72-7.69 (m, 2 H), 7.22-7.09 (m, 5 H),
6.73 (d, J = 8 Hz, 1 H), 5.19 (dd, J = 10.4 Hz J = 6.4 Hz, 1 H), 4.58 (s,
1 H), 3.60 (dd, J = 14.8 Hz, J =6.4 Hz, 1 H), 3.54 (dd, J = 14.4 Hz, J
=10.4 Hz, 1 H), 2.25-2.15 (m, 1 H), 0.96 (d, J = 6.4 Hz, 3 H), 0.88 (d, J
= 6.8 Hz, 3 H). 13C NMR (100M Hz, CDCl3): δ 175.61, 168.81, 167.95,
136.33, 134.28, 131.25, 128.82, 128.62, 126.99, 123.53, 57.33, 55.78,
34.96, 30.97, 18.91, 17.44. IR (neat) ν 3343, 2961, 1707, 1640, 1535,
1379, 717 cm-1. HRMS (ESI) [M+H+] m/z calcd for C22H23N2O5 395.1602,
found 395.1602. [α]D 20 = -76.3 (c = 0.3, MeOH). m.p. = 135-136 °C.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM thermal, optimization study, sealed tube used, optimized on solvent and
base, scalable
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Site-Selective C(sp3)-H Functionalization of Di-, Tri-, and Tetrapeptides
at the N-Terminus
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Gong, Wei; Zhang, Guofu; Liu, Tao; Giri, Ramesh; Yu, Jin-Quan
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of the American Chemical Society (2014), 136(48), 16940-16946

