$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(1):CAS_RN
$DATUM 920-66-1
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Arylation of
Dipeptides (Tables 1 and 2). To a microwave tube (5 mL) was added the
substrate (0.2 mmol), Pd(OAc)2 (0.005 or 0.01 mmol as indicated in Table
1 or 2), AgOAc (0.24 mmol), ArI (0.3 mmol), KF (0.6 mmol), and HFIP (1
mL) in air. The tube was sealed and heated to 100 °C. The mixture was
stirred for 20 h at 100 °C. Upon completion, the reaction mixture was
cooled to room temperature. To the mixture was added acetic acid (0.3 mL)
and EtOAc (3 mL). The mixture was filtered through a short Celite pad,
and the filtrate was concentrated under reduced pressure. The resulting
mixture was purified by preparative TLC, typically using hexane/ethyl
acetate/HOAc mixtures as the eluent. The arylated product as a solid. The
arylated product was typically obtained as a single diastereomer (d.r. >
20:1), as evidenced by 1H NMR and 13C NMR. Product: 2g; Pale yellow solid
(74% mono + 11% di). 1H NMR (400M Hz, CDCl3): δ 7.80-7.78 (m, 2 H),
7.73-7.70 (m, 2 H), 7.43 (d, J = 8 Hz, 2 H), 7.29 (d, J = 8 Hz, 2 H),
6.64 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 1 H), 5.18 (dd, J = 8.8 Hz, J = 7.2 Hz, 1 H), 4.57
(dd, J = 8.4 Hz, J = 4.4 Hz, 1 H), 3.63 (d, J = 8.8 Hz, 2 H), 2.25-2.18
(m, 1 H), 0.96 (d, J = 6.8 Hz, 3 H), 0.88 (d, J = 6.8 Hz, 3 H). 13C NMR
(100M Hz, CDCl3): δ 175.71, 168.36, 167.87, 140.59, 134.57, 131.07, 129.7
(q, J = 31.8 Hz), 129.24, 125.57 (q, J = 13.7 Hz), 123.71, 57.31, 55.31,
34.63, 31.00, 18.93, 17.45. IR (neat) ν 3286, 2966, 1710, 1647, 1539,
1380, 718 cm-1. HRMS (ESI) [M+H+] m/z calcd for C23H22F3N2O5 463.1476,
found 463.1475.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM thermal, sealed tube used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Site-Selective C(sp3)-H Functionalization of Di-, Tri-, and Tetrapeptides
at the N-Terminus
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Gong, Wei; Zhang, Guofu; Liu, Tao; Giri, Ramesh; Yu, Jin-Quan
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of the American Chemical Society (2014), 136(48), 16940-16946

