$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Arylation of
Dipeptides (Tables 1 and 2). To a microwave tube (5 mL) was added the
substrate (0.2 mmol), Pd(OAc)2 (0.005 or 0.01 mmol as indicated in Table
1 or 2), AgOAc (0.24 mmol), ArI (0.3 mmol), KF (0.6 mmol), and HFIP (1
mL) in air. The tube was sealed and heated to 100 °C. The mixture was
stirred for 20 h at 100 °C. Upon completion, the reaction mixture was
cooled to room temperature. To the mixture was added acetic acid (0.3 mL)
and EtOAc (3 mL). The mixture was filtered through a short Celite pad,
and the filtrate was concentrated under reduced pressure. The resulting
mixture was purified by preparative TLC, typically using hexane/ethyl
acetate/HOAc mixtures as the eluent. The arylated product as a solid. The
arylated product was typically obtained as a single diastereomer (d.r. >
20:1), as evidenced by 1H NMR and 13C NMR. Product: 2e; White solid (72%
mono + 12% di). 1H NMR (400M Hz, CDCl3): δ 7.79-7.76 (m, 2 H), 7.72-7.68
(m, 2 H), 7.13 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 2 H), 7.09 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 2 H), 6.73 (d,
J = 8.4 Hz, 1 H), 5.13 (t, J = 8.4 Hz, 1 H), 4.57 (dd, J = 8.4 Hz, J =
4.4 Hz, 1 H), 3.52 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 2 H), 2.25-2.15 (m, 1 H), 0.95 (d, J =
6.8 Hz, 3 H), 0.87 (d, J = 6.8 Hz, 3 H). 13C NMR (100M Hz, CDCl3): δ
175.59, 168.53, 167.91, 134.86, 134.49, 132.82, 131.12, 130.19, 128.78,
123.69, 57.29, 55.59, 34.23, 30.99, 18.95, 17.47. IR (neat) ν 3346, 2963,
1775, 1709, 1648, 1535, 1380, 717 cm-1. HRMS (ESI) [M+H+] m/z calcd
forC22H22ClN2O5 429.1212, found 429.1213. m.p. = 72-74 °C.
