$DATUM Ethyl Ester of
2-t-Butoxycarbonylaminomethylthiazole-4-carbonyl-2(1-(R)-amino-3-cyano-prop-1-yl)-thiazole-4-carbonyl-(S)-valyl-(S)-leucyl-(S)-proline
(9): A solution of methylester of
N-benzyloxycarbonyl-(R)-valyl-(R)-leueyl-(R)-proline (3 g, 6.3 mmol) in
methanol (50 ml) containing palladium on charcoal (5%, 500 mg) is
hydrogenated at 3 atm for 2h. After filtration from the catalyst and
evaporation the residue is dissolved together with
2-t-butoxycarbonyl-aminomethyl-thiazole-4-carbonyl-2(1-(R)-amino-3-cyano-prop-1-yl)(thazole-4-carboxylic
acid (2.93 g, 6.3 mmol, obtained by saponification of 8 in dioxane water
with 1 normal sodium hydroxide) in absolute dimethyl formamide (30 ml)
and cooled to - 4 °C. Diphenyl phosphonic azide (1.93 g, 7 mmol) and
triethylamine (0.8 g, 7.9 mmol) are added and the mixture is stirred for
3d at - 4 °C. After evaporation in vacuo, the residue is dissolved in
ethyl acetate is washed successively with 1 normal potassium hydrogen
sulfate (10 ml), 1 normal potassium hydrogen carbonate (10ml) and water
(20 ml). The organic layer is dried with magnesium sulfate and
evaporated. Medium pressure chromatography on silica gel (ethyl acetate)
of the residue gives 9. Yield 3.9 g, 80%. Rf = 0.22 (ethyl acetate);
[α]D20: +3.0° (c = 1.06, dichloromethane). C35H50N8O8S2(774.9) calc. C
54.25 H 6.50 N 14.46 S 8.27 found 54.20 6.58 14.23 8.21
1H-NMR(CDCl3/TMS): δ = 0.95 (m, 12H); 1.47 (s, 9H); 1.40-2.80 (m, 12 H);
3.75 (s, 3 H); 3.50-4.10 (m, 2 H); 4,45-5.05 (m, 5 H); 5.70 (m, 1H); 5.95
(m, 1 H); 7.60 (m, 1H); 7.98 (d, 1 H, J = 9 Hz); 8.23 (s, 1 H); 8.27 (m,
1H); 8.38 ppm (s, 1H).
